# ---- Data (never commit landed data; it's reproducible from source) ----
/data/bronze/
/data/silver/
/data/gold/
/data/mcp_audit.jsonl
/data/agent_runs/
/data/orchestration_runs/
!/data/samples/
*.parquet
*.duckdb
# F11 — guards against the PowerShell quoting accident that created a stray
# `data;C` directory at the repo root (an unquoted path argument containing a
# `;` got split by the shell, e.g. `data;C:\...`) — catches a recurrence of
# that exact shape without ignoring anything under the real /data/ tree above.
/data;*

# ---- Secrets / env ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Rust ----
target/
# F12 — gitignore has no inline-comment syntax; the line this replaced
# (`Cargo.lock  # keep for binaries...`) was the literal pattern
# "Cargo.lock  # keep for binaries..." and matched nothing, so Cargo.lock was
# never actually ignored despite the comment's intent. Made explicit instead:
# both Rust crates in this repo (services/stress-engine, services/ingestion)
# build binaries (each has a main.rs), and Cargo's own guidance is to commit
# Cargo.lock for binaries (reproducible builds) — so it is deliberately
# tracked, not ignored. Both are already committed; this comment exists so
# a future crate doesn't get its lockfile dropped by a copy-pasted line.

# ---- Node / frontend ----
node_modules/
.next/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# ---- Java / Spark ----
*.class
.gradle/
build/

